<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muhammad al-Tunisi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">at court c. 1803–<a href="/years/1812">1812</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Muhammad al-Tunisi was a North African scholar and traveller who lived at the court of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darfur-sultanate">Darfur Sultanate</a> from about 1803 to 1812, under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mohammed-al-fadl">Mohammed al-Fadl</a>. His account of Darfur's society, commerce and court is one of the most important sources on the sultanate. He described a prosperous court and a sophisticated commercial network.</p></div>
